    "title": "Control Board 4a: maintenance and the upkeep calendar",
    "why": "decisions/0171 §2.5, §1 and §12 (release 4, split in two with the session manager's OK): a workflow or a task with its own switch can be taken out of service on purpose, with why and a Back by. It's shut down in order, shows blue, its alarms are notices and Start skips it; Put back runs its check first. Windows set ahead go out and come back by themselves on the 5-minute watch, logged (late or missed, never silently). The upkeep calendar lists what's due, read from the code. Also Pulse #31: Database updates lists the tables and columns no code names, read only, where its case now opens. With the session manager's fixes: the pre-flight result line amber unless a line really tripped or a core host is down; the alarm list's filter as one dropdown button in the header; maintenance in the brand's river blue; Take out's length a Thresholds setting (control_maint_hours).",
